{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md collab/yang-clojure/1794790000000-engineer-d1-r14-companion-subset-retention.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"cat: collab/yang-clojure/1794790000000-engineer-d1-r14-companion-subset-retention.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md: No such file or directory\n# D1 r15 — dependency bundle prerequisite, partial\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit, promotion, corpus publication, bounded run, verification result, or reliance claim. This is a smaller partial than the requested items 1–2 checkpoint: neither item is complete.\n\n## Handoff discrepancy\n\nHEAD is `e4ac2114`. The only pre-existing tracked changes are the bounds draft and r12 static C1 pilot; r13 findings were untracked. The named r14 findings, the two named architect ruling files and the Jupiter `target/d1-r9b-*` retained store and outcomes are absent in this checkout. The available r9b findings describe 155/155 on Jupiter, not a store available here. This laptop has a separate `target/d1-r9e-retained-store/content.jing` (about 705 MiB) and the r9e/r9g pilot records; these are not substituted for the missing r14 publication or represented as the Jupiter store. The original §4.1 design and the available predecessor findings were consulted. The exact text of the missing rulings and r14's claimed retention work cannot be checked here. The user-supplied option (c) is the current instruction, but a retention owner remains undesignated.\n\n## Change\n\n`yang.correspondence-dependency` implements a JVM byte-preserving Jing bundle prerequisite: explicit relative path/byte-array inputs are materialized individually as schema-1 Base64 blobs; an addressed schema-1 index names each blob. Fetch validates the closed index and blob shapes, canonical Base64 and distinct safe relative paths; `dao.jing/get` checks content addresses. It refuses missing/malformed content and does not write or execute fetched bytes. The caller must identify dependencies: this mechanism does not establish that a bundle is a dependency closure, capture files automatically, perform rebinding, attest an execution environment, or claim that code is safe to run. No actual compiler bundle, profile, or recipe was published. No origins were generated.\n\nRed first: the new focused test initially failed to load the missing namespace. The focused dependency, existing text and lane tests then passed **9 tests / 76 assertions**, 0 failures/errors, including arbitrary bytes and close/reopen of a file-backed store, duplicate/unsafe path and missing-content refusals. `clojure -M:kondo --lint` on both new files: 0 errors, 0 warnings. `git diff --check` passed. Frozen `slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 is `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No full oracle suite was run.\n\nThe existing `test/yang/correspondence_lane.clj` already has an alternate measured runner returning aggregate `:steps`, and `correspondence_verification.clj` records those steps within its pilot result. The older `run-guest-machine` still discards its successful count. Neither observation establishes retained complete per-fixture two-lane evidence.\n\n## Remaining work, in order\n\n1. Recover the actual r14 state and normative rulings. Inventory and retain the exact executable frontend, compiler, runtime and transitive dependencies, grammar/options, expansion environment, transformations and admitted domain; capture the real recorded admissions and expansion attempts. Specify and implement verified rebind/replay, compatible host profile and refusal rules. Address the resulting profile and closure from the schema-1 recipe; test lossless retrieval and real reconstruction. The bundle above is only storage plumbing, not this result.\n2. Produce and retain cc3-compatible publishable C1 metadata and instruction-provenance records for each actual retained fixture, connected to its actual admission and roots; verify fetch and complete mappings. Do not invent missing origins.\n3. Construct semantic, stack and register artifacts, check each execution contract and its verifying derivation chain per fixture, and retain results.\n4. Capture successful instruction counts and complete drain/loss-checked two-lane traces with per-fixture evidence, respecting the retained origins and the final frozen bounds. Integrate these with independent reconstruction and separate verification publication.\n5. Complete measured finite bounds and owner-designated full-store retention; produce the workspace-relative subset and companion only from a closed, fetchable artifact graph. Preserve row-lane-only restriction until its bridge is implemented and verified. The current draft and pilots do not authorize a bounded verification run.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
