ng-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-retained-pilot.edn\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-carrier-check.edn\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-phase-pilot.edn\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-plan.edn\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-independent-claim-plan.edn\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-static-c1-pilot.edn\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794796000000-engineer-d1-r13-c1-continuation.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r5.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:19:TDD: the amended wrapper/NaN and profile-id tests first failed against the old class-strict implementation; the first replay test failed for missing helper; an attempted stamped-tree coverage assertion then failed because it incorrectly expected wrapper helpers to be marked, and was corrected to the post-port accounting. The diagnostic tests check the original `:line` key and retained scope/ordinal. The amended capture test passed 1 test / 7 assertions; the scoped capture-refusal test passed 1 test / 2 assertions; and the full pre/post-stamp reopened-store replay pilot passed 1 test / 6 assertions. The correspondence, text-profile and Clojure call-site battery passed 49 tests / 659 assertions. clj-kondo 2026.08.04 reported 0 errors and 0 warnings on the touched code/test files. Full oracle suite and tagged lanes were not run.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r4.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:17:This is a limitation of the stipulated initial plain `pr-str`/EDN profile for this admitted input, not a demonstrated change to the original compiler result and not a reason to weaken equality or invent an origin. The r3 root-only pilot did not test metadata/numeric fidelity and remains a feasibility observation only. Its old successful replay test was replaced by the explicit real-fixture refusal regression; it is not represented as an r4 passing gate. An architect/owner decision is needed on a replay-preserving representation/profile or on an explicitly revised admissible-input/fidelity rule; no such change was assumed here.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r4.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:27:Red-first: new profile namespace was initially missing; adding capture requirements first failed because `forms`, `call` and options lacked text captures; attempting the real fixture under the strict capture then exposed the numeric metadata fidelity failure. The failure was retained as a refusal regression, not converted to a successful reconstruction. The correspondence, text-profile, and Clojure call-site battery passed 49 tests / 638 assertions. The real-fixture refusal test passed 1 test / 5 assertions and the earlier static table/binding test passed 1 test / 12 assertions. clj-kondo 2026.08.04 reported 0 errors and 0 warnings across all touched code/test files. The full oracle suite and all tagged lanes were not run.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r2.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:10:- `yin.vm/materialize-tree!` persists each validated canonical row body separately by its root/row address. `yin.vm.encoder/source-envelope` and `project` supply recorded source-origin coordinates and marker rows; cc3 test's `cc3-oracle-binding` supplies the post-stamp translation. `kernel-compile` records admission coordinates before compilation. Exact retained expansion environment/attempt records and all reconstruction inputs remain unestablished; the recipe must not invent them.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r2.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:- Post-port rebind note `1794519755000-engineer-post-port-oracle-reverification.glm-5.3.findings.md` §item 3 was read from canonical collab. It pins Phase 3r `8456c2e9`: two wrapper applications, site extraction `[:operands 1 :operands 1 :value]`, translated wrapped-argument path `[3 1] [3 2]`, and two inserted applications per site. This is not an independent D1 reconstruction.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r3.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:`kernel-compile` has an opt-in input-capture argument; ordinary callers do not retain extra copies. A static pilot captures the *actual* fixture, forms, call, assembled program, compiler options, and source-origin coordinates from the live `:beta-eq-false` compilation. It stores the input, the actual validated row closure via `vm/materialize-tree!`, and C1 metadata in a file store, closes and reopens it, and fetches them. No guest lane runs and no new historical origin is assigned.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r3.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:13:A material replay hazard was found before asserting a recipe. Directly recompiling the decoded Jing `:program` produces a different root even though the decoded value compares equal: in the observed run original root `:segment/blake3-174be253477fc45e9cfc97b2feb271d76de682049c1c7ba9ad22f80d8c44bb4b`, decoded replay root `:segment/blake3-540da09d07af75a62b39c0d315a8cdfc8d3b947de6366975da2be34780c7bd45`. A dynamic map at program path `[48 4]` changed iteration order across the canonical codec; `yang.clojure/compile-constructed-collection` lowers the iteration order into operands. This is not a Jing corruption: the data compares equal, but collection iteration order is observable by this compiler.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r3.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:19:- The exact reconstruction profile and runnable interpreter have not been implemented and pinned. In particular, the ordering-preserving representation needs an explicit specified contract and per-input replay/refusal gate across all corpus fixtures; the one pilot is insufficient. The exact code-producing frontend/compiler/dependency and expansion environment/attempt closure still needs retention and a determination of which expansion events actually occur; do not invent an expansion record or assume a commit string is a retrievable closure.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794710000000-engineer-d1-r9d-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:5:`yang.correspondence-batch/corpus-index!` constructs an intermediate index of the six retained addresses and admission origin for each fixture, refusing non-passes, count disagreement, absent direct objects, mismatched fixture/admission/root and missing evidence fixture. It does not construct or verify the D1 record, executable recipe, row transitive closure, image contracts or trace completeness. The r9b progress record is bookkeeping, not a verification result. The exact compiler/interpreter dependency and expansion-attempt closure remain unestablished; inventing a profile or calling this index a complete recipe would conceal that gap. The two original architect ruling files named in the dispatch remain absent in this checkout; the r5 findings record the numeric rule but are not a substitute for the normative texts.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794705000000-engineer-d1-r9c-bounds-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:21:A separate exploratory static-size/heap script `target/d1-r9c-static-measure.clj` opened the scratch store and attempted to re-encode the four direct roles for all fixtures while sampling JVM used heap every 5 ms. It was interrupted before it emitted per-fixture results or a peak, so it supplies **no measurement or ceiling**. It also overlapped the standing tests, and its scope excludes row closures and lane execution; even a completed sample would not establish the tagged-run peak. The scratch script and incomplete log remain under `target/` for inspection. No tagged execution was involved.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:Worktree mirror only; no commit. **No complete bounds declaration, tagged verification result, or companion was produced.** The r9e retained store at `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and its 155-outcome record remain the inputs; retention location and ownership remain an owner decision. The frozen v1 evidence SHA-256 is `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:7:Design `1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` §6.3 states bounds must be published **before any tagged run**, while the r9f dispatch asks for retained-corpus C-lane trace measurements before the declaration and then a separate tagged verification under it. The earlier r9e dispatch also explicitly says no tagged run before the declaration. I initially treated measurement execution as distinct from a tagged verification run and executed the retained stamped `:minimal-last` tree on both lanes **before a complete declaration**. That execution did not follow §6.3's sequencing. It is an unbounded-preflight observation with a 4,000,000 step cap, not a passed bounded run, and it must not be represented as verification or a compliant bounds-governed sample. Once I noticed §6.3's broader wording, I stopped the next process while it was opening the store; it recorded no fixture. Whether the requested measurement is an explicit exception or bounds must come first needs clarification. The retained measurement file explicitly records `:pre-declaration-tagged-execution true`.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:23:After the r9f brief was repeated, the sequencing question remained unresolved. The resumed lane-measurement process was stopped before it reached a fixture; no additional tagged lane was run. Independent static work proceeded: `check-retained-trees!` re-fetches and validates both complete row closures under the recorded admission, refusing mismatched fixture, admission or root. After opening the retained store in a fresh process, the static sweep passed **155/155** with zero refusals; fixture IDs and both row counts match the r9e outcomes for every fixture. Its per-fixture progress is `1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-row-recheck.edn`, with log and resumable driver `target/d1-r9f-row-recheck.log` and `target/d1-r9f-row-recheck.clj`. This is a static second traversal, not the traversal required within the later tagged verification.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:17:At this stopping point `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` SHA-256 is `ea2b6829d6a33a5bfe32e312dc6b93e91e4181e633b9c46de45471e2227264a8`; `target/d1-r9b-store/content.jing` is 154,053,237 bytes. The batch log is `target/d1-r9b-batch-2.log` and the reopen check is `target/d1-r9b-check-2.log`. The check was run using `java -cp \"$(clojure -Spath -A:test)\" clojure.main target/d1-r9b-check.clj`; two preliminary attempts accidentally invoked the test alias's broad default suite and were interrupted, so they are not completed test results. The frozen table SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794314809000-architect-adoption-rounds-2-4-d1-scoping-r2.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:75:1. **The \"three-kind correspondence\" is LaTTe-oracle consumer logic, NOT a `yang.clojure` compiler surface, and it is ALREADY landed on `master`.**\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794314809000-architect-adoption-rounds-2-4-d1-scoping-r2.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:152:      :yang.correspondence/compiler-revision {:git-sha \"<commit>\" :source-sha256 \"<sha256>\"}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794314809000-architect-adoption-rounds-2-4-d1-scoping-r2.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:182:   1. Verify `:upstream-revision`, `:compiler-revision`, and `:recipe` digests against the checkout.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794314809000-architect-adoption-rounds-2-4-d1-scoping-r2.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:195:   - Clojure runtime/compiler cell-ref authenticity landed in `0b74b4bb`, `7a4b5fc9`, `bfe9a8d9` (merged via `ae91bb8d`).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794314809000-architect-adoption-rounds-2-4-d1-scoping-r2.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:244:     - **Impact**: None of `cc2`, `cc3`, `cc4`, or `D1` needs to edit `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`! All `yang.clojure` compiler C1 hooks landed in `cc1`. Keeping `cc2`–`cc4` and `D1` out of `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` guarantees **zero merge conflict** with the exception-track seat's `R3`/`R4` work.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:7:HEAD is `e4ac2114`. The only pre-existing tracked changes are the bounds draft and r12 static C1 pilot; r13 findings were untracked. The named r14 findings, the two named architect ruling files and the Jupiter `target/d1-r9b-*` retained store and outcomes are absent in this checkout. The available r9b findings describe 155/155 on Jupiter, not a store available here. This laptop has a separate `target/d1-r9e-retained-store/content.jing` (about 705 MiB) and the r9e/r9g pilot records; these are not substituted for the missing r14 publication or represented as the Jupiter store. The original §4.1 design and the available predecessor findings were consulted. The exact text of the missing rulings and r14's claimed retention work cannot be checked here. The user-supplied option (c) is the current instruction, but a retention owner remains undesignated.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:`yang.correspondence-dependency` implements a JVM byte-preserving Jing bundle prerequisite: explicit relative path/byte-array inputs are materialized individually as schema-1 Base64 blobs; an addressed schema-1 index names each blob. Fetch validates the closed index and blob shapes, canonical Base64 and distinct safe relative paths; `dao.jing/get` checks content addresses. It refuses missing/malformed content and does not write or execute fetched bytes. The caller must identify dependencies: this mechanism does not establish that a bundle is a dependency closure, capture files automatically, perform rebinding, attest an execution environment, or claim that code is safe to run. No actual compiler bundle, profile, or recipe was published. No origins were generated.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794795000000-engineer-d1-r15-upstream-construction.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:19:1. Recover the actual r14 state and normative rulings. Inventory and retain the exact executable frontend, compiler, runtime and transitive dependencies, grammar/options, expansion environment, transformations and admitted domain; capture the real recorded admissions and expansion attempts. Specify and implement verified rebind/replay, compatible host profile and refusal rules. Address the resulting profile and closure from the schema-1 recipe; test lossless retrieval and real reconstruction. The bundle above is only storage plumbing, not this result.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:Worktree mirror; no commit. The complete declaration, bounded corpus verification, D1 companion and verification result remain unfinished. The r9e store `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` remains uncommitted; its retention location and ownership remain an OWNER DECISION.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:`verify-retained-fixture!` now records row-fetch, direct-content-fetch, replay and gate elapsed times; the gate records tree, independent static, mutation and query phases. `1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-claim-phase-pilot.edn` records all 155 r9e fixtures passing the existing gate with 165 supplied queries and both guarded lanes. Each outcome is labeled `:pre-declaration true`; these pilot passes do not certify D1. The initial store open took 195,419 ms, separately. Maximum fixture time was 67,358 ms, with a 5 ms sampled process used-heap peak of 3,880,862,784 bytes. The draft records phase maxima and comparability limits. The r11 69,936 ms datum remains the larger full-fixture observation from the handoff; the previous 60,000 ms candidate was never frozen and is inadequate. No declaration ceiling was raised.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:17:`yang.correspondence-static/compare-static!` materializes the same retained tree in separate in-memory baseline and C1 stores, reconstructs and checks call-site markers from application occurrences, and times publication, load and a relation query. It is an exploratory static comparison: it does not reconstruct the compiler/recipe or complete provenance, does not run a guest, does not publish the relation as an index, and repeated calls in one JVM are not independent cold starts. Its progress file is `1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-static-c1-pilot.edn`; it is not a declaration or verification result.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-declaration-completion.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:19:The first fixture, `:minimal-last`, passed with 798 markers. Its store opening was 276,530 ms; its cold baseline projection, marker derivation, publication, loading, relation construction and query took 161, 214, 116, 73, 1 and 41 ms respectively. That process's 5 ms sampled used-heap peak was 3,434,817,888 bytes. A second batch opened the store in 248,522 ms and was stopped after 19 additional passes; the atomic progress file records **20 passes, 135 not run, zero refusals**. Its final process heap peak was not recorded because the batch was interrupted. These are observations for a limited comparison, not ceilings. To resume this exploratory preflight from the worktree, run `java -Xss64m -cp \"$(cat target/d1-r9e-classpath.txt)\" clojure.main target/d1-r12-static-c1-pilot.clj 135`; it selects only `:not-run` fixtures and writes incrementally. This scratch command is not the missing complete verification recipe.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794729000000-engineer-d1-r10-declaration-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:Status: **in progress; no complete declaration or bounded verification result**. Worktree mirror, no commit; the r9e store is `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and remains uncommitted with retention location/owner pending. The r9g explicit sequencing resolution authorizes pre-declaration pilots, with only a later declaration-governed run counting as verification.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794729000000-engineer-d1-r10-declaration-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:23:The corrected diagnostic (`target/d1-r10-baseline-diagnose-02.log`) found the original baseline assembly mismatch at the source-line metadata of the fixed, discarded trace-stream bootstrap: the two literal forms were structurally equal but came from different source files. The helper now permits metadata differences only for that exact discarded bootstrap, retaining strict fidelity for the rest; red-first tests also refuse equal maps with different iteration order. The first refusal remains recorded. The new trace-free comparison file `1794729000000-engineer-d1-r10-baseline-pilot-02.edn` (SHA-256 `d57b6a06f6a05e8cf2e47efa1ab1c3c4c6c13f52788d306da6137378e2784e92`) records 155 passes; both executions of each benchmark root agreed on step counts and values. Walker/semantic max baseline steps 1,679,842 / 927,761, with largest fixture-paired tagged-minus-baseline increases 864,640 / 470,888 and maximum ratios ~1.822 / ~1.810. These are separate benchmark roots/processes. The local path index is not C1/provenance, and sequential compile timings are not fresh-cache cold/warm experiments. The r9e admission is named only as the source of input, never asserted as the benchmark root's persisted origin.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-declaration-verifier-integration.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:Status: **partial; no complete bounds declaration, bounded corpus verification, D1 companion or verification result**. Worktree mirror; no commit. The retained r9e store under `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` stays uncommitted and its retention location/owner remains pending. The r9g sequencing resolution authorizes labeled pre-declaration pilots and requires any verification run to follow a frozen declaration.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-declaration-verifier-integration.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:23:`verify-retained-fixture!` now joins the r9e outcome to retained input,\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-declaration-verifier-integration.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:33:per-step checks apply only within each lane. The progress writer now attempts\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794728000000-engineer-d1-r9g-sequencing-resolution.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:Status: **in progress; not a verification result**. Worktree mirror; no commit. The r9g dispatch resolves sequencing for this round: tagged C-lane pilot measurements precede the declaration and are explicitly pre-declaration observations, not verification evidence; the bounded verification run follows the declaration. The r9f caution about a conflict was superseded by that explicit resolution. The retained store is `target/d1-r9e-retained-store`, uncommitted; retention location/owner remains pending.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794728000000-engineer-d1-r9g-sequencing-resolution.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:5:The r9f pilot in the actual progress file was `:minimal-last`, not `:beta-eq-false`. It is preserved and now labeled `:pre-declaration true`. The r9g first batch measured 25 more, including `:beta-eq-false`: 26 passes, 129 not run at that checkpoint. Every finalized measurement outcome receives `:pre-declaration true`, as checked in a red-first progress test. The progress record `1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-measurements.edn` is authoritative; batch logs under `target/d1-r9g-pilot-*.log` include sampled process heap maxima. A pilot measurement pass says both lanes halted and their ring trace drained without a detected evicted prefix; it is not an independent verifier result. The harness uses the retained stamped roots and r9e admission coordinates; it records exact `vm/step` calls, trace-record count, UTF-8 printed-EDN vector bytes, fetch/run/drain elapsed and per-batch 5 ms sampled process used heap. The 4,000,000-step limit is a pilot safety cap, not a bound-governed verification verdict. Heap samples may miss transient peaks and count the whole process, including store open; printed-EDN bytes are not heap occupancy or encoded Jing size. No assertion of per-record peak size or trace buffer byte capacity follows from that measurement alone.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794728000000-engineer-d1-r9g-sequencing-resolution.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:7:The separate reopened static second traversal is complete: `1794422563000-engineer-d1-r9f-row-recheck.edn` records 155 passes, 0 refusals, both row closure counts matching r9e; this does not replace a traversal in a tagged verification. Focused measurement/lane tests after the per-outcome label change passed 5 tests / 23 assertions. The changed label test failed before the implementation was updated. No complete declaration, bounded tagged verification, D1 recipe/record or verification/companion publication has yet been made. Exact executable/dependency and expansion closure and independent image/provenance checks are still required; do not invent these or claim verification from pilot observations.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794728000000-engineer-d1-r9g-sequencing-resolution.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:13:The additional static profile `1794728000000-engineer-d1-r9g-static-profile.edn` (SHA-256 `afc6ae799b6d4e3747855e292fc603570b75dfe605dd1fd2af6e239feeec6e9a`) also completed 155 passes. Per-tree maximum before/stamped: 10,732 / 12,193 rows; 42,848 / 46,005 occurrences; 12,085 / 12,987 applications; path depth 462 / 464; application path CBOR bytes 3,423,911 / 3,730,572. Max encoded input 4,254,284 bytes, snapshot 12,266,106, profile 1,102, evidence 6,334,093. Static profile sampled 3,776,231,752 bytes of used process heap. Details and caveats, including a missing-direct-object sentinel weakness in the original profiling script, are appended to the draft; all 930 direct addresses had been independently fetched after reopening in r9e, and fixture inputs/snapshots were explicitly checked in this pass. The script has been corrected for future use.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:1:# D1 r9e: fresh laptop admissions — static corpus complete; verification incomplete\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:Worktree mirror; no commit. This is a static-gate progress checkpoint, not a D1 verification result or authorization for reliance. The outcomes file is `collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e.outcomes.edn`; consult it for the current per-fixture state. The scratch store `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` must be retained, not cleaned: the owner decision on durable retention location and ownership is pending. It is uncommitted and is not a published durable service.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:7:The first batch completed 5 passes, and its test ran 1 test / 9 assertions with zero failures or errors. Batch 2 completed another 5; batch 3 completed another 25. Their separate post-close/reopen direct-address checks found 60/60 and 210/210 addresses respectively. That is not a complete post-reopen traversal of every row closure. The retained content log was 172,069,545 bytes at the end of batch 3. Per-batch logs are under `target/d1-r9e-batch-02.log` and `target/d1-r9e-batch-03.log`; `target/d1-r9e-batch.clj` runs the next batch and performs direct address checks after closing and reopening. Batch 4 completed 25 further passes, leaving 60 passes, 0 refusals and 95 not run; after close/reopen all 360 direct addresses were available. Its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-04.log`, the store measured 493,055,591 bytes, and its sampled process heap peak was 3,677,225,328 bytes. Batch 5 completed 25 more passes; its close/reopen found all 510 direct addresses. Its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-05.log`, store size 562,134,762 bytes and sampled process heap peak 3,546,214,336 bytes. Batch 6 completed 25 more passes; its close/reopen found all 660 direct addresses. Its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-06.log`, store size 634,626,686 bytes and sampled process heap peak 3,590,144,896 bytes. Batch 7 completed the remaining 45 passes. The full record is 155 passes, 0 refusals and 0 not run. After close/reopen, all 930 direct addresses were available; its log is `target/d1-r9e-batch-07.log`. The final store is 734,517,424 bytes. This batch sampled 3,599,774,656 bytes of used heap. The first batch did not publish a heap sample. Batch 2 sampled a 1,914,713,024-byte process used-heap peak; batch 3 sampled 2,183,660,952 bytes. The existing sampler reads `Runtime.totalMemory - freeMemory` at 5 ms intervals: it can miss transient peaks, includes unrelated process heap, is not a live-object census and excludes the post-batch reopen and all C-lane execution. These observations are not a complete bounds declaration.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e-fresh-admissions.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:15:The focused first batch test passed 1 test / 9 assertions; later batches invoked the same gate directly, with explicit reopen address checks, and recorded every outcome. clj-kondo on all four correspondence sources, four correspondence tests and `latte_oracle_test.clj` reported 0 errors and 0 warnings. No code changes or new red-first tests were made this round. The full oracle suite was not run. No companion or verification artifact was fabricated: the complete executable/dependency/expansion closure, image and instruction provenance verification, lane counters and completeness checks, and full bounds remain unfinished. Retention location and owner remain pending; preserve `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and the outcomes file together.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r7.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:9:`fetch-tree!` fetches and validates the complete addressed row closure with an explicit row limit, rejecting missing/malformed rows and limit exceedance. A first attempt to store a nested AST snapshot failed honestly because `dao.jing.cbor` refuses nesting deeper than 128. The pilot now materializes pre-stamp and stamped trees as individually addressed rows and reconstructs them after reopening, rather than changing Jing's contract or raising that limit.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r7.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:25:The complete versioned recipe with executable compiler/profile/dependency and expansion-attempt closure is still not pinned or retained. The required instruction-provenance side records and image derivation chains for these particular admitted oracle trees have not been produced or independently verified; the landed linker publisher is not, by itself, proof that its publication origin and this harness's `[:source :program ...]` admission are interchangeable. Fixture-to-admission scoping, the aggregate record's exact representation, artifact inventory and durable discovery still need completion. The output of `check-fixture!` cannot stand in for these. Do not create a placeholder D1 record or manufacture origin/expansion information to fill the gaps. The row-lane-only restriction remains.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
