{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'profile|reconstruction-input|expansion|attempt|rebind|compile-program' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj src/cljc/yang/correspondence* collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yang/correspondence_batch.clj:35:                                   [:input :snapshot :evidence :profile :root :stamped-root]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_batch.clj:165:                                   (select-keys addresses [:input :snapshot :evidence :profile :root :stamped-root]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_text.clj:7:(def profile\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:18:    :yang.correspondence.recipe/profile :yang.correspondence.recipe/input-roles\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:34:  \"Check the closed schema and basic shapes, without resolving the profile.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:39:       (jing/segment-address? (:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile x))\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:108:  \"Store a structurally valid recipe after its profile and coverage are present.\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:113:  (doseq [address [(:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile recipe)\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc:145:                             (:yang.correspondence.recipe/profile recipe)\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:98:   `constructors` is the profile's set of context-state constructor names.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:175:  \"Derive the profile's state constructor names from retained context forms.\"\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:24:Consequently **the oracle evidence schema's exact identifier, field names, and canonical-source-hash algorithm/profile are unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides from the oracle's accepted record**. This document specifies the envelope around that record and its verification obligations, not an independently invented replacement site-table schema. “OracleEvidence” below means the entire accepted versioned oracle value, verbatim, including its site ids, argument-shape declarations, fixture linkage, trace schema, and version. Before durable implementation is accepted, the inventory must pin its concrete file, commit, schema identifier/version, validator, and derivation entry point. Absence of that pin blocks durable acceptance; it does not block the oracle round.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:38:- `origin` identifies the actual admission or generation event. Admitted syntax uses `[:source medium batch-token j]`; generated syntax uses `[:expansion expansion-record-address]`. Generated post-expansion trees must not be mislabeled as original source or given a fabricated expansion address. If a no-op expansion retains an admitted tree, the original source origin remains valid; “post-expansion” names the pipeline boundary, not proof that a generating event occurred.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:39:- An origin is supplied by the admitting/generating composition. Two separately admitted identical sources have different origins; two identical applications in one tree have different paths; two expansion attempts with identical output have different producing records. Replaying a single recorded admission is different from admitting the same text again.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:41:The implemented origin validator accepts exactly the source and expansion shapes (`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:938-958`). `vm/occurrences` returns `[root path node-id]`, one per place, with origin fixed by the composition; it does not return full keys or count only distinct row ids (`vm.cljc:1589-1609`).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:65:Finalize paths only after macro expansion, generated-name canonicalization, wrappers, module/SCC assembly, and tail marking that determine the named tree. Source-level annotations alone cannot cover generated calls (base ruling R2 at line 17). Low-level functions returning fragments may defer finalization until an owning root and origin exist; each executable/publication ingress must invoke the common finalizer. A frontend cannot claim adoption by marking just its parser or user-call lowering arm.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:69:Macro expansion already records input root, call path, macro root, parent, output and attempt (`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:997-1000,1062-1119`). However, final tail marking and stand-in lowering happen later (`:1255-1260`). The implementation inventory must resolve how final published roots are related to these expansion outputs. Whether the existing event/record adapters already provide the complete final-root correspondence is **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides**. Do not assume an intermediate output record identifies every occurrence in the final assembled tree, and do not mint a fake `:expand` merely to satisfy the shape.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:91:The composition supplies two non-nil plain-data tokens: `evidence-scope-token` names the recording/fixture scope; `compilation-token` names this particular instrumented compilation in that scope. `member-index` is a nonnegative integer. They are explicitly recorded inputs, not inferred from source hash, host object identity, time, lane name, or callee. Both oracle C lanes execute the SAME compiled artifact with the same tokens; a separate compilation gets another token. Replay uses the recorded tokens. A source hash alone would collapse distinct attempts.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:93:This is a precise proposed spelling for the still-unfrozen oracle implementation. It is **not** a third legal persisted occurrence origin: `vm/occurrence-origin?` must continue rejecting it. An EDN evidence file may preserve an ephemeral id as evidence of that run; that does not convert it into a portable code occurrence. Persisted C1 side tables and expansion links require real ruled origins.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:116:| Code lowering profiles | Read, and verify unchanged code output. A separately versioned provenance recipe names any new side mapping. | Revise the relevant code profile if a pinned lowering rule or emitted code changes, even if execution grammar does not. A side-only addition must not masquerade as validation by the old derivation verifier. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:119:| Frontend catalog revision/profile | Change the frontend revision and relevant annotation/support profile when its publication/coverage promise changes. | Existing revision pinning and conflict/incompatible refusal remain; keep SPI 1 unless its actual request/response protocol changes. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:132:| Clojure `compile-form`, `compile`, `compile-program`, `lower-unit`: `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2021,2164,2839,2993` | Cover native and argument-vector/outcome compilation, library/adapters, linked unit wrapping and global publication. Finalize at executable roots, after expansion. Existing fragment APIs need not invent origins. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:135:| Legacy PHP `compile-program/compile`: `yang/php.cljc:640-685` | Additional live frontend, not retired by the presence of ANTLR. Annotate all generated combinator/wrapper applications too. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:141:| Macro pipeline: `yin/vm/macro.cljc:997-1005,1062-1119,1196-1261` | Keep expansion attempt provenance, resolve final-root ownership, annotate generated occurrences and retain retrievable expansion records. Post-expansion is a required integration point. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:157:“Side tables are additive” is the compatibility policy, not permission to skip republishing coverage evidence. **Unannotated persisted artifacts remain loadable under their supported existing code contracts.** A provenance-requiring query returns missing provenance/refuses credit; it never invents identity from names, hashes, arities, values or source lines. Old provenance may be reconstructed only when the actual admission/expansion inputs are retained, and the result is a newly verified artifact.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:172:Preserve the existing failure categories: malformed canonical content fails structural validation; wrong bytes/address fails hash verification; unknown execution contract refuses load; differing lowering profile reports profile mismatch or `:unverified-derivation`; wrong recomputed output reports derivation mismatch (`vm.cljc:283-285`; `ledger.cljc:156-180`; `linker.cljc:2175-2215`). New evidence-specific failures must be distinguishable: unsupported C1/evidence version, missing provenance, bad occurrence, incomplete coverage, wrong source/adaptation hash, missing lane, ambiguous correspondence, stale declared site, or reconstruction mismatch.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:204:`inputs` names the retrievable source/adaptation/fixture/profile inputs required by the recipe, including the inlined adapter and declarations that the oracle actually hashed. A repository commit string alone is not a fetchable reconstruction input. `roots` names the produced code trees. Expansion records and admitted source-envelope identities required by the bindings must be in the retrievable input closure. The input/source artifacts may be data blobs; they must not be represented as UAST addresses unless they actually are UAST.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:211: :yang.correspondence.recipe/profile <address of exact reconstruction profile>\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:217:The recipe profile pins frontend/compiler revision, grammar/options, expansion environment and recorded origins/attempts, all code-producing transformations, source canonicalization, site-table derivation, and lowering/provenance rules. The consumer must implement that exact recipe/profile. A missing upstream canonicalization rule is not repaired by choosing a plausible hash. The exact oracle schema identity remains the dependency in §1.1.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:219:`origin-bindings` is an added relation binding evidence-local sites to actual durable occurrences; **it is not a replacement attribution table**. It preserves the oracle's ephemeral ids literally. Validate every endpoint, reconstructed tree and path. A site's mapping must be unique within the claimed compilation. Multiple replay records can name the same durable occurrence only where they explicitly replay the same admission; distinct admissions must remain distinct. An oracle run without durable expansion/source records cannot be promoted merely by changing `:ephemeral` to `:expansion`. It may remain useful oracle evidence without a durable binding. To accept a relying consumer, reproduce the actual compilation under recorded durable admissions/expansions and verify its correspondence; do not retroactively assert an unrecorded event.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:229:3. Reconstruct the source/adaptation compilation under the exact recipe, using recorded source admissions and expansion attempts; recompute final roots and eligible occurrence sets. Recompute the oracle's canonical-source-hash using its exact rule.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:233:7. Publish a separate verification result naming D1's address, recipe/profile, verifier revision, inputs, outcomes and evidence. D1 cannot mark itself “verified”. The first additional consumer's acceptance must cite this completed result.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:262:Build a portable replay fixture containing the SAME source or source-derived CST, grammar/options, compiler/profile revision, canonical naming inputs, source-medium/batch/member coordinates, and expansion environment/attempt inputs. The source origin contract explicitly makes these coordinates supplied plain data (`code-as-tuples.md:405-437`; `vm.cljc:938-958`).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:268:- For expansion fixtures, identical expansion-record addresses under replayed identities and identical producing-record chains. Normalize neither origin nor generated names away after the fact.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:276:**Clojure.** Inventory native/argument-vector/outcome compile options, `compile` vs `compile-program`, `compile-form` callers, macro expansion, `lower-unit`, `library-for`, direct walker/datoms/rows lanes, REPL single/multi-form and linked runtime publication. Show a non-oracle production fixture traversing the full pipeline, including macro-generated and helper calls. Republish `clj` and `yang.call` on each host. Oracle-specific stamping is instantiation #1 only; it does not close this brief. Anchors: `yang/clojure.cljc:2021-2034,2164-2200,2791,2839-2862,2993-3021`.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:284:Each brief's acceptance bundle contains: exact producer/artifact checklist; input/commit/profile pins; C1 coverage counts and root/hash invariance; four-host results and cross-host equality report; correctness battery results; before/after budgets and measurements; legacy-load/missing-provenance refusal; and D1 verification result if it relies on correspondence. No frontend can satisfy this bundle merely by running the oracle test.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:320:| Maximum input rows, occurrences, A, D and total path bytes | Derive from the pinned static corpus; reject over-bound traversal before instrumentation. Include generated/bundled prelude expansion, not only source calls. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:335:| Clojure | Native and argument-vector/outcome roots, macro outputs, guest library, linked `clj/yang.call`, repeated REPL admissions; `A_clj + L_clj + sum(P_f)` plus retained expansion/input closure | Nested/multi-arity/indirect/helper/tail calls in both production and oracle-specific fixtures; oracle owns its existing ceilings |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:348:| Duplicate content / admission | Two identical applications at different paths; identical roots at two batch indices; identical source admitted twice; identical expansion outputs from two attempts. Distinct K where required, shared content allowed. Tamper one origin/root/path and refuse cross-borrowed evidence. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:349:| Macro generation | A call introduced only by expansion, nested expansions, repeated expansion attempts, final tail/stand-in transformations, and unexpanded source retained in the same compilation. Reconstruct real producing records; raw-source site counts cannot pass. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:359:| Stale table and schema | A declared id never observed in a trace produces the recorded diagnostic; unsupported versions, fabricated expansions, extra/conflicting/incomplete marker rows, missing retained inputs and wrong profiles produce distinct failures. Do not silently treat malformed evidence as an honest unexecuted site. |\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:372:2. After the cell-ref sweeps/J2 land, refresh the exact producer, validator, artifact and host inventory; identify every changed contract, every read-only dependency, and any required format revision. Resolve final expansion-root ownership and native provenance completeness.\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:157:    (into {} (map (fn [[op]] [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:185:                      (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:191:   adapters and the VM primitives' published profiles as the native names.\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:194:   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:216:                      (concat (keys vm/primitive-profiles)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:218:                              ;; inline by compile-program under :outcomes true\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:262:         ast (yang/compile-program program true arg-vector-opts)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:399:            (yang/compile-program [form]))))))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:915:                 host-constant? binderify free-vars vars mk-fresh subst- rebinder subst])\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:975:        (eval '(declare subst- rebinder subst))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1299:        builder (yang/compile-program (into (yang/library-for forms) forms) true arg-vector-opts)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1716:(defn- kernel-attempt\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1732:  (let [ast (yang/compile-program '[((fn [x] x) 1)] true arg-vector-opts)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1734:               (kernel-attempt\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1756:  (kernel-attempt\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1798:  (kernel-attempt\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2216:   APPLICATION EXPRESSIONS, post-macroexpansion (R2), and derive the site\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2529:                      (map (fn [[op profile]] [(clojure.core/symbol \"stream\" (name op)) profile])\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2530:                           module/stream-profiles))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2535:         compiled (yang/compile-program program true opts)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2537:         ;; post-macroexpansion (R2), with the mechanically derived site\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2555:         (assoc :reconstruction-input\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2572:    (assoc (kernel-attempt\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3035:        compiled (kernel-attempt #(kernel-compile fixture run-scope admission-ordinal))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3435:      :rule \"caller-side site ids at compiled-AST application expressions (post-macroexpansion); records [guest-function arity caller-site]; ambient arities credit only through adapter-declared ambient-literal sites; delegations and the :gate-site/none entry site never credit\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3618:;; cc3: oracle integer sites bound to post-expansion C1 occurrence keys\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3771:  \"Bind each stamped oracle site id to its post-expansion C1 key\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3919:      (testing \"replay: rebinding one retained compilation is the same history\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3966:            \"every bound key is a validated post-expansion C1 occurrence\"))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4284:    (is (every? #(string? (get (:reconstruction-input compiled) %))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4301:        ast (yang/compile-program program true opts)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4352:        input (:reconstruction-input compiled)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4365:                            :profile (jing/materialize! handle correspondence-text/profile)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4374:            (is (= correspondence-text/profile (jing/get reopened (:profile addresses) ::missing)))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4397:        input (:reconstruction-input compiled)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4500:                          :input (jing/materialize! handle (:reconstruction-input compiled))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4501:                          :profile (jing/materialize! handle correspondence-text/profile)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4510:            stored-profile (jing/get reopened (:profile addresses) ::missing)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4521:            _ (when-not (= correspondence-text/profile stored-profile)\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4522:                (throw (ex-info \"Profile missing or changed\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :profile})))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4528:                (:id fixture) (yang/compile-program replay-program true replay-options) (:root stored-snapshot))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
