{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'run-guest-machine' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; rg -n 'expansion|attempt|origin' collab/yang-clojure/179470*findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"1736:                    (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast (oracle-registry) :walker 1)\n2573:             #(let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n2601:    (:max-depth (compiler-test/run-guest-machine-depth\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794705000000-engineer-d1-r9c-bounds-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:Design §4.2 requires a retrievable D1 record and recipe, image contract and derivation checks, independent reconstruction and instruction mapping, complete scoped lanes, and a separate result. The scratch outcomes retain six segment addresses per admission, not the D1 record/recipe or a pinned executable and expansion dependency closure. `check-fixture!` expressly excludes admission authenticity, executable-image derivations and trace completeness; `attributed?` assumes pre-scoped complete lane traces and trusts the supplied `:complete?` flag. The runner `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` `run-guest-machine` discards the successful instruction counter, so it cannot report actual guest instructions as required. The r9 and r7 findings describe the still-missing provenance/image checks. Row-lane-only remains the stated restriction.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794705000000-engineer-d1-r9c-bounds-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:15:The two specifically named architect ruling files were not present in this worktree under the supplied names; r5 records the numeric fidelity amendment, but that secondary account is not a substitute for the normative originals. Obtain the original rulings before asserting their full compliance.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794705000000-engineer-d1-r9c-bounds-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:21:A separate exploratory static-size/heap script `target/d1-r9c-static-measure.clj` opened the scratch store and attempted to re-encode the four direct roles for all fixtures while sampling JVM used heap every 5 ms. It was interrupted before it emitted per-fixture results or a peak, so it supplies **no measurement or ceiling**. It also overlapped the standing tests, and its scope excludes row closures and lane execution; even a completed sample would not establish the tagged-run peak. The scratch script and incomplete log remain under `target/` for inspection. No tagged execution was involved.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:5:The batch pass outcome now retains the six actual segment addresses returned by persistence: input, snapshot, evidence, profile, root and stamped-root. The batch record refuses a pass missing any of these addresses. A storage delta of zero is permitted because deduplicated replay can add no bytes. The record remains bookkeeping, not a verification result. Each admission is generated by the existing fresh run and recorded with its origin; no historical coordinates are invented.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:7:Scratch progress is `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` (SHA-256 at this stopping point `cfffefb46cebc49c74a44b6db739d32bb5e8bd631d3b382d9d9b6faf773f1f3b`), with its store at `target/d1-r9b-store/content.jing` (26,292,420 bytes). These are local scratch, not published retention. The first process was interrupted after seven recorded passes; a fresh process reopened the store and progress file and added one pass. A separate fresh process then reopened the store, fetched all 48 addresses for the eight passes, and checked that each input and snapshot origin equalled the recorded admission origin. This demonstrates process-interruption resume for this sample, not a power-loss test or the completed corpus.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:15:The existing run resumed with a 25-fixture batch, using the same outcomes file and store, with spot checks enabled. The invocation completed successfully (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors); all 25 new outcomes passed. A separate process reopened the store and fetched all six retained addresses for each of the 33 passes, and checked that each fetched input and snapshot origin matched its recorded admission origin. Its summary was **155 fixtures: 33 pass, 0 refused, 122 not run; 198 addresses checked**. This is still a partial static corpus rebuild, not a verification result.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:17:At this stopping point `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` SHA-256 is `ea2b6829d6a33a5bfe32e312dc6b93e91e4181e633b9c46de45471e2227264a8`; `target/d1-r9b-store/content.jing` is 154,053,237 bytes. The batch log is `target/d1-r9b-batch-2.log` and the reopen check is `target/d1-r9b-check-2.log`. The check was run using `java -cp \"$(clojure -Spath -A:test)\" clojure.main target/d1-r9b-check.clj`; two preliminary attempts accidentally invoked the test alias's broad default suite and were interrupted, so they are not completed test results. The frozen table SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:23:The next 25 fixtures passed the static gates (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-3.log`). A fresh process reopened the shared store, fetched all six retained addresses for each pass, and checked that the input and snapshot origins matched the recorded admissions (`target/d1-r9b-check-3.log`): **155 fixtures, 58 pass, 0 refused, 97 not run; 348 addresses checked**. This remains a partial static rebuild, not a verification result. The progress file SHA-256 at that checkpoint was `802386972c1e8fbd128511e9be18a3bfe6d2593aa6a97e143f02e8d9c46b9b48`; the store was 461,259,401 bytes. The frozen table SHA-256 was still `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No code changed in this continuation and no commit was made. The undeclared bounds, verifier limitations, and missing tagged run and publications described above remain open.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:33:The final batch completed the 155-fixture static rebuild (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-7.log`). The progress record has **155 pass, 0 refused, 0 not run**. Every pass records its fresh admission origin and six retained addresses, including input and snapshot. A separate fresh process reopened the final store, fetched all **930** recorded addresses, and checked each input and snapshot origin against its recorded admission (`target/d1-r9b-check-final.log`). This verifies retrieval and origin equality for those objects, not admission authenticity, trace completeness, or durable published retention.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
