{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794800000000-engineer-d1-r16-recipe-closure.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r16 — retained-input inventory; closure remains open\n\nWorktree mirror; no commit. This is a partial investigation, not a recipe, publication, verification result, or reliance claim. Preserve \"'`target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and its outcomes together. The requested r14 findings, two named ruling files, and Jupiter r9b store are absent here, as already recorded in r15. This laptop'\"'s r9e corpus is a separate run.\n\n## What the capture actually retains\n\nThe r9e capture implementation in \"'`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, `kernel-compile`, records the actual fixture, forms, call, assembled program, options, EDN representations of the latter four, and the source admission coordinate. The six addressed roles written by `d1-corpus-static-gate!` are evidence, input, text profile, binding snapshot, pre-stamp root and stamped root. The snapshot carries bindings, C1 rows and context constructors. The stored profile is `yang.correspondence-text/profile`: JVM and serialization/reader details, not an executable compiler profile. The producer replay calls the checkout'\"'s \"'`yang/compile-program`, then checks the resulting root; equality under that checkout does not establish which compiler bytes were used originally or provide a fetchable compiler and transitive runtime.\n\nThe capture path does not include a compiler byte bundle, grammar revision, independently recorded expansion environment or an expansion-event log. The program and options may include expanded library forms and actual options; they are valuable inputs but do not establish the missing producer history or prove a complete dependency closure. This observation does not assert that this particular compilation necessarily invoked the row-native expander. In particular, its events cannot be invented from a resulting tree. `yin.vm.macro/expand-batch` has explicit event/attempt records when that expander is used, while `expand` returns only the tree packet. Any claim of no relevant expansion attempts also needs evidence, not inference from absent records.\n\nThe r9e findings name `ccd3648dc4e1877dfed0e507d6f6c0971115bfc2` plus uncommitted measurement helpers. The commit exists; the current HEAD is `e4ac21142397d27bf6627121c29ddfb57a602970`. The historical and current tracked versions of `yang/clojure.cljc`, `yin/vm/macro.cljc`, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, and `deps.edn` compare equal, and these files are currently clean. This is useful candidate-source evidence, not proof of the complete original runtime or all historical uncommitted bytes, and the commit is not an addressed retrievable dependency bundle. The r15 byte bundle implementation stores supplied bytes and explicitly does not prove completeness.\n\n## Consequences and next work\n\nNo compiler closure was bundled or attached to a recipe: doing so on the available evidence would silently assert the missing provenance. First recover the original executable/classpath and actual expansion context or event records, including evidence of any inapplicable stages. Establish the real transitive dependency inventory and verified replay/rebind semantics, then use the r15 store for the identified bytes and reference it from the profile addressed by the recipe. If those original facts cannot be recovered, a newly captured compilation under explicit recorded coordinates and environment is a distinct admission, not a retroactive history of r9e.\n\nThe C1 rows in the snapshot are not by themselves cc3'\"'s published, verified metadata and instruction-provenance side records. No image derivation checks or complete per-fixture trace evidence were generated this round. The legacy \"'`run-guest-machine` still discards its counter; `yang.correspondence-lane/run-measured!` separately reports aggregate steps and `read-